hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1676","\nNarrated to us Naṣr ibn ʿAlī, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dāwūd narrated to us, on the authority of al-Walīd ibn Jamīʿ, from Laylā bint Mālik, from her father, and from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Khalād, from Umm Waraqah, that the Prophet of Allāh (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Go with us so that we may visit the martyr.\""\n\nHe (ﷺ) granted her permission to give the adhān and to lead the women of her household in the obligatory prayers. She had memorized the Qur"""""
